Tabz: forward-fix the webhook + nightly receipt backfill safety net

Forward fix for the issue that required Ashley's manual backfill earlier today.

1) Webhook: broaden order_id extraction
   The post-rebrand Tabz events nest the order under data.order with the
   ID at data.order.id (not data.order_id). extractOrderId now checks
   that path plus a couple of other shapes seen in the OpenAPI spec.
   Effect: new paid events will populate healnowOrderId at webhook time
   and fetch the receipt immediately — no recovery pass needed.

2) Webhook: accept order::* events alongside prescription::*
   The OpenAPI spec only documents order::pending and order::paid as
   webhook events. We see prescription::* events too (likely a
   backwards-compat layer Tabz still ships), but pinning ourselves to
   only prescription::* means a deprecation flip would silently drop
   every payment. Now we handle both.

3) Nightly receipt backfill workflow
   GitHub Actions cron at 06:00 UTC (1am EST / 2am EDT) calls
   /api/healnow-backfill for the prior day with dryRun=false. Idempotent
   — only touches items whose paidStatus is set but receipt blob is
   missing (the recovery path added earlier today). Catches any future
   webhook payload-shape changes within 24h instead of leaving receipts
   blank indefinitely.
